Package: rcpgsd
Type: Package
Title: Regional Consistency Probability under Group Sequential Designs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given  = "Gosuke",
    family = "Homma",
    role   = c("aut", "cre"),
    email  = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com"
  )
Description: Computes regional consistency probabilities (RCPs) for
    multi-regional clinical trials (MRCTs) with a time-to-event endpoint
    analysed by a group sequential design. Method 1 and Method 2 of the
    Japanese Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare (MHLW) guidance are
    evaluated at each interim and final analysis, on the log hazard ratio
    scale or on the hazard reduction scale, conditional on stopping for
    efficacy at that analysis. Closed-form solutions based on the
    multivariate normal distribution of the overall and regional log hazard
    ratio estimates are provided, with numerical integration for the exact
    hazard reduction criterion and Monte Carlo simulation for verification.
    A patient-level simulation of event-driven trials with piecewise uniform
    accrual, exponential event times and exponential drop-out, using the
    log-rank test, the Pike or Peto estimate of the overall hazard ratio and
    regional Cox models, is provided to assess the accuracy of the normal
    approximation.
    Efficacy and futility boundaries can be taken from 'gsDesign' or 'rpact'
    design objects, with binding or non-binding futility boundaries.
    Consistency thresholds adjusted for the inflation of the null RCP caused
    by early efficacy stopping are also provided. For planning, the accrual
    by region with delayed regional starts is constructed under the overall
    accrual plan, the expected regional event proportions are derived from
    the accrual pattern, and the smallest proportion of events in the region
    of interest that achieves a target RCP is computed.
